    {
      "name": "FiniteField2m",
      "crate_name": "finite-field",
      "doc": "Finite field manager for GF(2^m) with a given primitive (irreducible) polynomial px(x)\nCoefficients of px are given as bits over GF(2): px(x) = sum px[i] x^i, px[m]=1, px[0]=1 typically.\nElements are represented as u16 bit patterns of polynomial basis (low->high), so m must be <= 15.\nThis is chosen for performance and WASM friendliness; can be generalized to u32 if needed.\n\nExample (GF(2^4), px = x^4 + x + 1):\nlet px = [1,1,0,0,1].map(GFp::<2>); // low->high\nlet field = FiniteField2m::new(&px);\nlet a = field.alpha_pow(1); // α\nlet b = field.alpha_pow(3); // α^3\nlet c = field.mul(a, b);    // α^4 = α + 1 (mod px)",
      "fields": [
        "m: usize",
        "n: usize",
        "px_bits: u32",
        "exp: Vec < u16 >",
        "log: Vec < i32 >"
      ],
      "enum_variants": [],
      "dto_candidate": false,
      "dto_enabled": false
    }
  ],
